ed up so it  doesn't go  automatically you sort of overheat if  you start feeling frustrated if you  start feeling  um  worried or out of control  then you know you have to remove  yourself from a situation  take time take deep breaths and  basically recalibrate  and keep your cool karen moss thank you  so much for being with us here tonight  you're welcome thank you for having me  up next this week's winners and losers  in the media see what the editors of  media had had to say about fox news  you're watching brian ross investigates  on the law and crime trial network  time now for this week's winners and  losers in the media as chosen by the  editors of mediaite and we're joined by  aidan mclaughlin the editor-in-chief of  meteorite which like the law and crime  trial network is part of the dan abrams  media group and aiden you've chosen as a  winner this week fox news now given all  the rants and misinformation why are  they a winner  that's right so putting aside all the  criticisms of fox news that we've made  on this on this segment repeatedly and  putting aside what you think of the  network's politics it goes without  saying that fox news is the most watched  thing on cable news uh it draws an  audience that is far bigger than msnbc  and cnn often far bigger than msnbc and  cnn combined um that has been the case  this week  on friday which is typically a pretty  soft day for cable news networks no show  on fox news drew less  than a million viewers  which is a sizable audience uh cnn and  msnbc were far behind cnn didn't even  draw uh more than 700 000 viewers for  any single show  even their top-rated shows um so it was  really a strong ratings week for fox  news  and that comes at a time when all of  cable news audiences are down so the fox  the fact that fox is still pulling in a  really sizable audience is a sign of  their influence uh and their continued  success and suggests they're just  shrugging off the criticism because it  works  right i mean i think fox news that's  been their play uh since its inception  um you know no matter how many times uh  the new york times op-ed page uh runs a  lengthy piece criticizing uh fox news um  as a danger to democracy uh viewers  continue to tune in um and are in fact  probably spurred by that um so i think  fox news sees the prophets continuing to  to come in and the audience continuing  to be there uh and they really don't  care about any of that criticism a lot  of times that criticism is justified um  so you know i wouldn't say that that's  necessarily a good thing but the  audience continues to tune in  and for this week's loser you've chosen  the former cbs 60 minutes correspondent  laura logan who hasn't been seen much on  the air since she made these comments  about dr faki on fox  what you see on dr fauci this is what  people say to me that he doesn't  represent science to them he represents  joseph mengele dr joseph  the doc the nazi doctor who did  experiments on jews during the second  world war and in the concentration camps  and so she has disappeared from the  airwaves since that  right uh this is a good example of what  is being aired on fox news not being  worthy of a win uh despite uh the  audience still being there uh laura  logan uh was once revered journalist for  60 minutes  um she took to appearing on fox news a  lot lately in the last year uh and  pushed a series of conspiracy theories  what you saw there was her comparing dr  anthony fauci to an infamous nazi doctor  of joseph mengele after those comments  which prompted a lot of outrage uh  criticism and calls for her firing she  disappeared from the air at fox news now  she was never employed by fox but she  appeared frequently as an unpaid guest  on the network and actually hosted  documentary show on fox nation now she  hasn't appeared on fox news since uh we  reported on mediaite uh on monday that  she had also been dropped by her  longtime agent uh who was at united  talent agency or uta so not only is she  no longer appearing on fox news she's  also been dropped by her agency which is  a pretty big deal for any journalist and  means that it's going to be hard to see  where lar logan is going to be able to  get her news out now um that she's  basically fully independent and has no  representation i doubt any you know the  traditional networks are going to be  hosting her uh fox news certainly has  signaled that they're not going to be  hosting her anymore on their airwaves um  so yeah i mean it's a serious loss for  for you know a once revered journalist  and a a stunning fall from grace and  from prestige  right i mean laura logan was you know  was a very very prestigious journalist  when she was at 60 minutes and you know  it was a bit of a long time coming  she made a series of controversial  comments on fox news this was just the  latest and the most controversial that  got her kicked off well hey mclaughlin  thank you so much for being with us  tonight as always your picks of the  winners and losers and thanks to all of  you for watching us we'll see you back  here again next week on the law and  crime trial network  [Music]  you
 

